Given the following text and a relational triplet extracted from it:

Text: You should not use prednisone if you are allergic to prednisone.
You should not use prednisone if you have a systemic fungal infection.
To make sure prednisone is safe for you, tell your doctor if you have or have ever had:
an infection of any kind, including tuberculosis, hepatitis B, herpes infection of the eye, or a fungal infection;
Diarrhea has no clear cause.
Time is spent in the tropics.
Prednisone can wake up a parasite infection.
The parasite infection is amebiasis.
The parasite infection is threadworm.
malaria, especially cerebral malaria (malaria affecting the brain);
liver disease, such as cirrhosis;
kidney disease;
heart disease, heart failure, high blood pressure or low potassium levels;
an underactive thyroid;
diabetes;
osteoporosis;
glaucoma or cataracts;
stomach ulcers, ulcerative colitis, diverticulitis, or a history of bleeding in the stomach or bowel;
myasthenia gravis (a condition that causes muscle weakness); or
depression, mood swings or another mental health condition.
Long-term steroid use can cause bone loss.
Your risk is higher if you smoke.
Triplet: ["prednisone", "increased risk in", "smokers"]

The relation 'increased risk in' in the triplet is defined as 'The subject drug poses a higher risk of adverse effects or complications in patients who fall into the group specified by the object entity.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Choose a relation whose meaning and subject/object direction match the triplet even if the wording differs; choose 'None of the above' only if no candidate fits. Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'has side effect more likely in': The subject drug is more likely to cause the specified adverse effect or reaction in the population or group specified by the object entity.
B. 'has side effect': The subject drug may cause the adverse effect or symptom specified by the object entity.
C. 'has serious side effect': The subject drug may cause the serious or potentially dangerous adverse effect specified by the object entity that requires medical attention.
D. 'use with caution in': The subject drug may be unsafe or require medical supervision for patients who have the condition or characteristic specified by the object entity.
E. 'has side effect frequency': The subject drug may cause the adverse effect specified by the object entity with the frequency indicated.
F. None of the above.

Answer:
